{
  "bookKey": "acts",
  "chapter": 1,
  "format": 1,
  "basis": {
    "1": "I made the first account, Theophilus, about everything Jesus began doing and teaching",
    "2": "until the day he was taken up, after giving directions by the Sacred Life-breath to the chosen commissioned ones.",
    "3": "And after he suffered, he presented himself alive with many definitive proofs, being seen by them over the course of forty days and discussing things about God’s Reign.",
    "4": "While he was staying with them, he directed them not to leave Jerusalem but to “wait for the Father’s promise, which you heard about from me,",
    "5": "since while John immersed in water, you will be immersed in the Sacred Life-breath not many days from now.”",
    "6": "Then, when they had gathered, they started asking him, “Lord, are you reinstating the reign to Israel at this time?”",
    "7": "But he said to them, “It’s not for you to know the periods or times which the Father has set by his own authority,",
    "8": "but you will receive power when the Sacred Life-breath comes over you, and you will be my witnesses in Jerusalem and in all Judea, Samaria, and to the farthest land.”",
    "9": "After saying these things, while they were watching, he was lifted up, and a cloud took him from their sight.",
    "10": "As they were gazing into the heavens while he went, suddenly, two individuals stood beside them in white clothing.",
    "11": "They said, “Men, Galileans, why are you standing looking up at the heavens? This same Jesus who was taken up from among you into the heavens will come back exactly the same way you watched him going into the heavens.”",
    "12": "Then they returned to Jerusalem from the Mount of Olives, which is near Jerusalem, a Shabbat’s journey away.",
    "13": "When they went into the city, they went up to the upper room, where they were staying: Peter, John, Jacob, and Andrew; Philip and Thomas; Bar-Talmai and Matthew; Jacob, son of Alphaeus and Simeon who was called Zealous; and Judah son of Jacob.",
    "14": "By unanimous agreement, they all attended constantly to prayer, together with some women, including Miriam the mother of Jesus, as well as his brothers.",
    "15": "During that time, standing up among the Family (in the middle of a crowd of about 120 people), Peter said,",
    "16": "“Men, Family, it was necessary for the scripture to be fulfilled, in which, through the mouth of David, the Sacred Life-breath foretold about Judah, the one who guided those who seized Jesus,",
    "17": "because he had been counted among us and received a share of this role of service.",
    "18": "He later acquired a field using the reward for his unjust act, and ending up face down, he burst open in the middle, and all his guts poured out.",
    "19": "It became known to all who resided in Jerusalem, so the field came to be called Hakeldama” (which in their own language means ‘Field of Blood’).",
    "20": "“You see, it was written in the book of Psalms, ‘His farmhouse should become desolate, and no one should reside in it,’ and ‘Another should receive his role of supervision.’",
    "21": "Therefore, it is necessary for one of the men who have accompanied us the whole time of the Lord Jesus’ comings and goings among us,",
    "22": "beginning from John’s immersion until the day he was taken up from us, for one of them to become a witness to his Rising Up along with us.”",
    "23": "They nominated two people, Joseph called Barsabbas (also known as Justus) and Matthias.",
    "24": "Praying, they said, “You, Lord, who know everyone’s hearts, make it clear which one of these two you have chosen",
    "25": "to receive the role of this service and commission which Judah sidestepped to move on to his own role.”",
    "26": "They assigned them lots, and the lot fell to Matthias, so he was counted together with the Eleven commissioned ones."
  },
